# Day 51 – Product Discovery & Sprint Planning

## Overview
Today marked the beginning of the capstone phase of the ABTalks 60 Days Claude AI Challenge.

Instead of jumping directly into development, I focused on discovering the right problem, validating the project idea, defining the product scope, and creating a complete roadmap for building and deploying a polished v1.0 product over the next 9 days.

---

## Project Selected

### JobTrack AI
An AI-powered Job Search & Application Tracking Platform designed for students and job seekers.

### Problem
Many students apply to dozens of jobs but struggle to track applications, interviews, resume versions, and progress efficiently.

### Solution
A centralized dashboard that helps users:

- Track job applications
- Manage interview schedules
- Organize resume versions
- Monitor application progress
- View analytics and insights
- Improve job search productivity

---

## V1 Features

### Dashboard
- Applications Overview
- Interview Tracking
- Offers & Rejections
- Success Metrics

### Application Manager
- Company Name
- Job Role
- Date Applied
- Status Tracking

### Resume Manager
- Resume Versions
- Notes & Updates

### Interview Tracker
- Upcoming Interviews
- Feedback Records

### Analytics
- Conversion Funnel
- Success Rate
- Performance Insights

### AI Insights
- Job Search Recommendations
- Application Improvement Tips

---

## Out of Scope

To avoid scope creep, the following features are intentionally excluded:

- ATS Integrations
- LinkedIn Scraping
- Email Automation
- Multi-user Accounts
- Payment System
- Complex Backend Infrastructure

---

## Deliverables Created

### Product Requirements Document (PRD)
Defined:
- Problem Statement
- User Personas
- Functional Requirements
- User Flows
- Success Metrics

### Implementation Blueprint
Created a detailed Day 52–60 execution roadmap including:
- Objectives
- Features
- File Structure
- Testing Plans
- Daily Milestones

### Project Pitch Deck
Prepared presentation content covering:
- Problem
- Solution
- Features
- Technical Approach
- Future Scope
- Vision

---

## Key Learnings

- Product success starts with clear planning.
- Scope management is critical.
- A smaller finished product is better than a larger unfinished product.
- Defining success criteria early reduces future confusion.
- Product discovery helps prevent building unnecessary features.

---

## Day 10 Success Criteria

- Fully Deployed Application
- Responsive UI/UX
- Core Features Functional
- AI-Powered Insights
- GitHub Repository Complete
- Demo Screenshots Available
- Production-Ready v1.0

---

## Next Steps

Tomorrow I will begin translating the PRD into a working product architecture and implementation plan as I continue building JobTrack AI toward a deployable v1.0.

